From: Producdevity <y.gherbi.dev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cnss2: allow native userspace without the Android daemon

The stock device tree enables cnss-daemon-support. CNSS then advertises two
WLFW clients, although a native Linux session has no Android cnss-daemon.
Provide a boot parameter to select the kernel-only client arrangement.
The default preserves the device tree policy.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/cnss2/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/cnss2/main.c
@@ -2372,11 +2372,16 @@
 	del_timer(&plat_priv->fw_boot_timer);
 }
 
+static bool daemon_support = true;
+module_param(daemon_support, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(daemon_support,
+		"Honor device tree support for the Android CNSS daemon");
+
 static void cnss_init_control_params(struct cnss_plat_data *plat_priv)
 {
 	plat_priv->ctrl_params.quirks = CNSS_QUIRKS_DEFAULT;
-	if (of_property_read_bool(plat_priv->plat_dev->dev.of_node,
-				  "cnss-daemon-support"))
+	if (daemon_support && of_property_read_bool(
+		plat_priv->plat_dev->dev.of_node, "cnss-daemon-support"))
 		plat_priv->ctrl_params.quirks |= BIT(ENABLE_DAEMON_SUPPORT);
 
 	plat_priv->ctrl_params.mhi_timeout = CNSS_MHI_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT;
